                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17959"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_24"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The vagina (TS:24-TS:28). The developing vagina is subdivided into upper vagina and sinovaginal bulb (or lower vagina), however only the upper vagina will become the vagina in the adult (Kurita 2010). The sinovaginal bulb is a transient structure only seen during development. The sinovaginal bulb is derived from the urogenital sinus epithelium (and is therefore often called the sinus vagina). The adult vagina (TS:28) is derived from the upper vagina (TS:24-TS:27), and is derived from the paramesonephric duct of female.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:18986</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>vagina</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18986"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The vagina (TS:24-TS:28). The developing vagina is subdivided into upper vagina and sinovaginal bulb (or lower vagina), however only the upper vagina will become the vagina in the adult (Kurita 2010). The sinovaginal bulb is a transient structure only seen during development. The sinovaginal bulb is derived from the urogenital sinus epithelium (and is therefore often called the sinus vagina). The adult vagina (TS:28) is derived from the upper vagina (TS:24-TS:27), and is derived from the paramesonephric duct of female.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20638775</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18987 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18987">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18986"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38161"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_24"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The upper vagina (uv) (syn: Mullerian vagina, upper part of vagina) (TS:24-TS:27) is comprised of epithelium, lamina propria, muscle and adventitia. Also contains vasculature (TS:24-TS:27) and nerves are seen from birth (TS:27). Derived from paramesonephric duct of female.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mullerian vagina</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>upper part of vagina</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:18987</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>upper vagina</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18987"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The upper vagina (uv) (syn: Mullerian vagina, upper part of vagina) (TS:24-TS:27) is comprised of epithelium, lamina propria, muscle and adventitia. Also contains vasculature (TS:24-TS:27) and nerves are seen from birth (TS:27). Derived from paramesonephric duct of female.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18988 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18988">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18682"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_25"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The glans penis (glp) (syn: penile glans) (TS:25-TS:28) is the distal part of the penis. The glans penis lies internally within the preputial space and externally is completely surrounded by the prepuce. The glans can be exposed when the prepuce is retracted. The distal part of the penile urethra is located within the glans penis. From TS:25-TS:27, is comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans penis. At TS:28, is comprised of corpus cavernosum glandis (two, linear corpora cavernosa, dorsally and ventrally located within the glans penis), corpus cavernosum urethra (linear erectile tissue ventral to the urethra), male urogenital mating protuberance (MUMP), os penis and lamina propria (stroma or connective tissue) and covered with skin. The glans penis is comprised of regions; the MUMP ridge (which encircles the glans and is comprised of a ridge (distal) and a groove (proximal) the MUMP ridge groove), and proximal to the ridge is the glandular ridge. The urethral meatus (the opening of the male penile urethra) is located at a ventral midline cleft in the MUMP ridge close to the distal tip of the glans penis (~1mm from the tip).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>penile glans</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:18988</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>glans penis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18988"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The glans penis (glp) (syn: penile glans) (TS:25-TS:28) is the distal part of the penis. The glans penis lies internally within the preputial space and externally is completely surrounded by the prepuce. The glans can be exposed when the prepuce is retracted. The distal part of the penile urethra is located within the glans penis. From TS:25-TS:27, is comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans penis. At TS:28, is comprised of corpus cavernosum glandis (two, linear corpora cavernosa, dorsally and ventrally located within the glans penis), corpus cavernosum urethra (linear erectile tissue ventral to the urethra), male urogenital mating protuberance (MUMP), os penis and lamina propria (stroma or connective tissue) and covered with skin. The glans penis is comprised of regions; the MUMP ridge (which encircles the glans and is comprised of a ridge (distal) and a groove (proximal) the MUMP ridge groove), and proximal to the ridge is the glandular ridge. The urethral meatus (the opening of the male penile urethra) is located at a ventral midline cleft in the MUMP ridge close to the distal tip of the glans penis (~1mm from the tip).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18989 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18989">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38171"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17969"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18682"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The prepuce of male (pce) (TS:24-TS:28) is the external part of the penis that completely surrounds the glans penis. The glans can be exposed when the prepuce is retracted.  Contains the preputial glands and mesenchyme of prepuce and surrounded by skin. Part of the genital tubercle of male (TS:24) and from TS:25 part of penis. Derived from preputial swelling of male (TS:21-TS:23). The preputial gland ducts drain into the preputial space. From TS:28, prepuce is comprised of skin containing hair follicles, preputial gland (paired), which drain into the preputial space and prepuce lamina propria (stroma or connective tissue).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>EMAPA:30634</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:18989</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>prepuce of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The prepuce of male (pce) (TS:24-TS:28) is the external part of the penis that completely surrounds the glans penis. The glans can be exposed when the prepuce is retracted.  Contains the preputial glands and mesenchyme of prepuce and surrounded by skin. Part of the genital tubercle of male (TS:24) and from TS:25 part of penis. Derived from preputial swelling of male (TS:21-TS:23). The preputial gland ducts drain into the preputial space. From TS:28, prepuce is comprised of skin containing hair follicles, preputial gland (paired), which drain into the preputial space and prepuce lamina propria (stroma or connective tissue).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


