                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18680"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The glans of female genital tubercle (TS:23-TS:24) is the distal part of the genital tubercle of female, comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans of female genital tubercle. Derived from distal genital tubercle of female. The distal end of the phallic urethra of female is located within the glans, including the urethral plate epithelium of female and part of the urethral tube epithelium of female. Becomes the glans clitoris at TS:25, when genital tubercle of female becomes clitoris.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:19170</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>glans of female genital tubercle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19170"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The glans of female genital tubercle (TS:23-TS:24) is the distal part of the genital tubercle of female, comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans of female genital tubercle. Derived from distal genital tubercle of female. The distal end of the phallic urethra of female is located within the glans, including the urethral plate epithelium of female and part of the urethral tube epithelium of female. Becomes the glans clitoris at TS:25, when genital tubercle of female becomes clitoris.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


