    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19294 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19294">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18682"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_25"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The penile body (syn: body of penis, crus penis) (TS:25-TS:28) is the proximal part of penis. Connected to the glans penis at a right angle bend. Contains within it, the proximal part of the penile urethra. Comprised of paired corpora cavernosa, corpus cavernosum urethra and lamina propria (stroma, connective tissue).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>body of penis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>crus penis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:19294</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>penile body</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19294"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The penile body (syn: body of penis, crus penis) (TS:25-TS:28) is the proximal part of penis. Connected to the glans penis at a right angle bend. Contains within it, the proximal part of the penile urethra. Comprised of paired corpora cavernosa, corpus cavernosum urethra and lamina propria (stroma, connective tissue).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19296 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19296">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30977"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The scrotum (TS:28-28) is located at the base of the penis and comprised of skin (epidermal layer of scrotum (comprised of basal layer and stratified layer), dermal layer of scrotum (comprised of hair follicle and sweat gland), septum of scrotum (syn: scrotal seam)), vasculature and nerve of scrotum. Derived from scrotal fold (TS:24-TS:27).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:19296</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>scrotum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_19296"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The scrotum (TS:28-28) is located at the base of the penis and comprised of skin (epidermal layer of scrotum (comprised of basal layer and stratified layer), dermal layer of scrotum (comprised of hair follicle and sweat gland), septum of scrotum (syn: scrotal seam)), vasculature and nerve of scrotum. Derived from scrotal fold (TS:24-TS:27).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


