    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28697 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28697">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38166"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18995"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The epithelium of pelvic urethra of male (TS:23-TS:28) is the innermost layer of the pelvic urethra, a stratified epithelium lining the lumen. It is subdivided into dorsal and ventral. It is also subdivided into three epithelial cell layers; superficial, intermediate and basal cell layer of dorsal/ventral pelvic urethra.  At TS:23, the epithelium of dorsal pelvic urethra of male is also comprised of urogenital sinus ridge of male and rest of dorsal epithelium of pelvic urethra of male. The urogenital sinus ridge becomes the verumontanum in males from TS:24. Cytokeratin 14 and Cadherin 1 are markers of all layers of the epithelium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28697</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>epithelium of pelvic urethra of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The epithelium of pelvic urethra of male (TS:23-TS:28) is the innermost layer of the pelvic urethra, a stratified epithelium lining the lumen. It is subdivided into dorsal and ventral. It is also subdivided into three epithelial cell layers; superficial, intermediate and basal cell layer of dorsal/ventral pelvic urethra.  At TS:23, the epithelium of dorsal pelvic urethra of male is also comprised of urogenital sinus ridge of male and rest of dorsal epithelium of pelvic urethra of male. The urogenital sinus ridge becomes the verumontanum in males from TS:24. Cytokeratin 14 and Cadherin 1 are markers of all layers of the epithelium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28703 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28703">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38167"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18995"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of male (mlplur) (TS:23-TS:28) is located between the epithelium and muscle layers. Contains smooth muscle cells and mesenchymal/fibroblastic/stromal cells, blood vessels and nerves and mesenchymal pads of male (TS:25-TS:27). Subdivided from TS:23-TS:28 into dorsal and ventral. Subdivided from TS:25-TS:28, into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa and submucosa.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28703</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28703"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of male (mlplur) (TS:23-TS:28) is located between the epithelium and muscle layers. Contains smooth muscle cells and mesenchymal/fibroblastic/stromal cells, blood vessels and nerves and mesenchymal pads of male (TS:25-TS:27). Subdivided from TS:23-TS:28 into dorsal and ventral. Subdivided from TS:25-TS:28, into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa and submucosa.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28709 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28709">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38168"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18995"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The muscle layer of pelvic urethra of male (muplur) (syn: muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of male) (TS:23-TS:28) is the thicker layer of smooth muscle towards the outside of the pelvic urethra. Subdivided into dorsal/ventral (to TS:27). Marked by proteins expressed by smooth muscle cells, such as smooth muscle alpha actin (Acta2).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of male</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28709</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>muscle layer of pelvic urethra of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28709"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The muscle layer of pelvic urethra of male (muplur) (syn: muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of male) (TS:23-TS:28) is the thicker layer of smooth muscle towards the outside of the pelvic urethra. Subdivided into dorsal/ventral (to TS:27). Marked by proteins expressed by smooth muscle cells, such as smooth muscle alpha actin (Acta2).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28747 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28747">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30901"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_23"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urethra of female (TS:23-TS:28). From TS:23 to TS:27, urethra of female is comprised of pelvic urethra of female and phallic urethra of female. At TS:28, urethra of female is comprised of pelvic urethra of female and clitoral urethra of female (syn: external urethra).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28747</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urethra of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urethra of female (TS:23-TS:28). From TS:23 to TS:27, urethra of female is comprised of pelvic urethra of female and phallic urethra of female. At TS:28, urethra of female is comprised of pelvic urethra of female and clitoral urethra of female (syn: external urethra).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30903"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28747"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38161"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_23"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The pelvic urethra of female (PLUR) (syn: cranial urethra, internal urethra) (TS:23-TS:28) is part of urethra of female. Cranially joined to the bladder and caudally joined to the phallic urethra of female (TS:23-TS:27) which becomes the clitoral urethra (TS:28). Comprised of epithelium (subdivided into 3 layers), mesenchymal layer (subdivided into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa, submucosa (TS:25-28) and also contains mesenchymal pad of female (TS:25-TS:27)), muscle layer and adventitia. Also contains vasculature and nerve of pelvic urethra of female, and neural crest derivative of pelvic urethra of female (TS:25-TS:27). Also contains ventral epithelial bud of female and female urethral gland bud (TS:24-TS:26), which become urethral gland of female pelvic urethra (TS:27), which develop from the epithelium of pelvic urethra of female. The pelvic urethra of female (TS:28) also contains a rhabdosphincter as part of the muscle layer of pelvic uretha of female. In the TS:28 male, the rhabdophincter is part of the prostatic urethra.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cranial urethra</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>internal urethra</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28753</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>pelvic urethra of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The pelvic urethra of female (PLUR) (syn: cranial urethra, internal urethra) (TS:23-TS:28) is part of urethra of female. Cranially joined to the bladder and caudally joined to the phallic urethra of female (TS:23-TS:27) which becomes the clitoral urethra (TS:28). Comprised of epithelium (subdivided into 3 layers), mesenchymal layer (subdivided into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa, submucosa (TS:25-28) and also contains mesenchymal pad of female (TS:25-TS:27)), muscle layer and adventitia. Also contains vasculature and nerve of pelvic urethra of female, and neural crest derivative of pelvic urethra of female (TS:25-TS:27). Also contains ventral epithelial bud of female and female urethral gland bud (TS:24-TS:26), which become urethral gland of female pelvic urethra (TS:27), which develop from the epithelium of pelvic urethra of female. The pelvic urethra of female (TS:28) also contains a rhabdosphincter as part of the muscle layer of pelvic uretha of female. In the TS:28 male, the rhabdophincter is part of the prostatic urethra.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28759 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28759">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38163"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The epithelium of pelvic urethra of female (TS:23-TS:28) is the innermost layer of the pelvic urethra, a stratified epithelium lining the lumen. It is subdivided into dorsal and ventral. It is also subdivided into three epithelial cell layers; superficial, intermediate and basal cell layer of dorsal/ventral pelvic urethra.  At TS:23, the epithelium of dorsal pelvic urethra of female is also comprised of urogenital sinus ridge of female and rest of dorsal epithelium of pelvic urethra of female. The urogenital sinus ridge becomes the sinovaginal bulb in females from TS:24. Cytokeratin 14 and Cadherin 1 are markers of all layers of the epithelium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28759</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>epithelium of pelvic urethra of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28759"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The epithelium of pelvic urethra of female (TS:23-TS:28) is the innermost layer of the pelvic urethra, a stratified epithelium lining the lumen. It is subdivided into dorsal and ventral. It is also subdivided into three epithelial cell layers; superficial, intermediate and basal cell layer of dorsal/ventral pelvic urethra.  At TS:23, the epithelium of dorsal pelvic urethra of female is also comprised of urogenital sinus ridge of female and rest of dorsal epithelium of pelvic urethra of female. The urogenital sinus ridge becomes the sinovaginal bulb in females from TS:24. Cytokeratin 14 and Cadherin 1 are markers of all layers of the epithelium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28765 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28765">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38164"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of female (mlplur) (TS:23-TS:28) is located between the epithelium and muscle layers. Contains smooth muscle cells and mesenchymal/fibroblastic/stromal cells, blood vessels and nerves and mesenchymal pads of female (TS:25-TS:27). Subdivided from TS:23-TS:28 into dorsal and ventral. Subdivided from TS:25-TS:28, into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa and submucosa.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28765</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28765"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The mesenchymal layer of pelvic urethra of female (mlplur) (TS:23-TS:28) is located between the epithelium and muscle layers. Contains smooth muscle cells and mesenchymal/fibroblastic/stromal cells, blood vessels and nerves and mesenchymal pads of female (TS:25-TS:27). Subdivided from TS:23-TS:28 into dorsal and ventral. Subdivided from TS:25-TS:28, into lamina propria, muscularis mucosa and submucosa.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28771 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28771">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38165"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28753"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female (muplur) (syn: muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of female) (TS:23-TS:28) is the thicker layer of smooth muscle towards the outside of the pelvic urethra. Subdivided into dorsal/ventral (to TS:27). At TS:28, subdivided into smooth muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female and rhabdosphincter of female (syn: striated muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:28771</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_28771"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female (muplur) (syn: muscularis propria of pelvic urethra of female) (TS:23-TS:28) is the thicker layer of smooth muscle towards the outside of the pelvic urethra. Subdivided into dorsal/ventral (to TS:27). At TS:28, subdivided into smooth muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female and rhabdosphincter of female (syn: striated muscle layer of pelvic urethra of female).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


