    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29220 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29220">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_35702"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17969"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The preputial swelling of male (pps) (syn: preputial fold of male, early prepuce of male) (TS:21-TS:23). Two lateral swellings develop on the sides of the genital tubercle at TS:21 and grow medially and ventrally. These swellings enclose the preputial glands. Comprised of skin of male preputial swelling, preputial gland of male, and mesenchyme of male preputial swelling.  At TS:24, when the two preputial swellings join/fuse together at the ventral midline of the genital tubercle of male, they become the prepuce of male.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>early prepuce of male</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>preputial fold of male</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:29220</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>preputial swelling of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29220"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The preputial swelling of male (pps) (syn: preputial fold of male, early prepuce of male) (TS:21-TS:23). Two lateral swellings develop on the sides of the genital tubercle at TS:21 and grow medially and ventrally. These swellings enclose the preputial glands. Comprised of skin of male preputial swelling, preputial gland of male, and mesenchyme of male preputial swelling.  At TS:24, when the two preputial swellings join/fuse together at the ventral midline of the genital tubercle of male, they become the prepuce of male.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


