    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29252 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29252">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_38179"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17969"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The glans of male genital tubercle (TS:23-TS:24) is the distal part of the genital tubercle of male, comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans of male genital tubercle. Derived from distal genital tubercle of male. The distal end of the phallic urethra of male is located within the glans, including the urethral plate epithelium of male and part of the urethral tube epithelium of male. Becomes the glans penis at TS:25, when genital tubercle of male becomes penis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>EMAPA:29288</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:29252</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>glans of male genital tubercle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_29252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The glans of male genital tubercle (TS:23-TS:24) is the distal part of the genital tubercle of male, comprised of skin and mesenchyme of glans of male genital tubercle. Derived from distal genital tubercle of male. The distal end of the phallic urethra of male is located within the glans, including the urethral plate epithelium of male and part of the urethral tube epithelium of male. Becomes the glans penis at TS:25, when genital tubercle of male becomes penis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


