                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_22"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_23"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The labial swelling (LSW) (TS:22-TS:23). Two lateral swellings develop ventrally, at the base of the genital tubercle of female. Comprised of skin, mesenchyme and developing vasculature of labial swelling. At TS:24, becomes the labial fold. Part of the female external genitalia and female reproductive system. Scrotal swellings are larger than labial swellings.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:30423</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>labial swelling</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30423"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The labial swelling (LSW) (TS:22-TS:23). Two lateral swellings develop ventrally, at the base of the genital tubercle of female. Comprised of skin, mesenchyme and developing vasculature of labial swelling. At TS:24, becomes the labial fold. Part of the female external genitalia and female reproductive system. Scrotal swellings are larger than labial swellings.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


