    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30870 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30870">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17379"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_19"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_21"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The primitive bladder (PBL) (syn: cranial urogenital sinus) (TS:19-TS:21) is the anterior/cranial part of the urogenital sinus, lined with urothelium, located anterior to the attachment point of the common nephric duct/nephric duct at the urogenital sinus ridge. At TS:19 the primitive bladder is an epithelial lined cavity comprised of urothelium of primitive bladder (upbl, endoderm-derived epithelium) and the adjacent mesenchyme of primitive bladder (mpbl, mesoderm-derived). From TS:20-TS:21 it is also comprised of developing vasculature of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21), outer layer of primitive bladder (either serosa of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21) or adventitia of primitive bladder) and from TS:21, muscle layer of primitive bladder. From TS:20, the mesenchyme of primitive bladder is subdivided into inner and outer layers. Becomes bladder (TS:22-TS:28).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cranial urogenital sinus</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:30870</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>primitive bladder</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30870"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The primitive bladder (PBL) (syn: cranial urogenital sinus) (TS:19-TS:21) is the anterior/cranial part of the urogenital sinus, lined with urothelium, located anterior to the attachment point of the common nephric duct/nephric duct at the urogenital sinus ridge. At TS:19 the primitive bladder is an epithelial lined cavity comprised of urothelium of primitive bladder (upbl, endoderm-derived epithelium) and the adjacent mesenchyme of primitive bladder (mpbl, mesoderm-derived). From TS:20-TS:21 it is also comprised of developing vasculature of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21), outer layer of primitive bladder (either serosa of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21) or adventitia of primitive bladder) and from TS:21, muscle layer of primitive bladder. From TS:20, the mesenchyme of primitive bladder is subdivided into inner and outer layers. Becomes bladder (TS:22-TS:28).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30873 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30873">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31509"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_37978"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30870"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_21"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urothelium of primitive bladder (upbl) (syn: epithelium of primitive bladder, epithelial layer of primitive bladder) (TS:19-TS:21) is the urothelial layer lining the lumen of the primitive bladder, comprised of a stratified epithelium of different epithelial cell types depending on stage, a subpopulation of which expresses Uroplakin. Derived from cloacal endoderm. At TS:19-TS:20 the upbl is comprised predominantly of P-0 cells and very few undifferentiated epithelial cells. At TS:21 the upbl is comprised of P-0 cells (usually on the luminal surface) and intermediate cells. Becomes the urothelium of bladder at TS:22.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>epithelial layer of primitive bladder</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>epithelium of primitive bladder</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:30873</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urothelium of primitive bladder</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30873"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urothelium of primitive bladder (upbl) (syn: epithelium of primitive bladder, epithelial layer of primitive bladder) (TS:19-TS:21) is the urothelial layer lining the lumen of the primitive bladder, comprised of a stratified epithelium of different epithelial cell types depending on stage, a subpopulation of which expresses Uroplakin. Derived from cloacal endoderm. At TS:19-TS:20 the upbl is comprised predominantly of P-0 cells and very few undifferentiated epithelial cells. At TS:21 the upbl is comprised of P-0 cells (usually on the luminal surface) and intermediate cells. Becomes the urothelium of bladder at TS:22.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30876 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30876">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31500"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30870"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_19"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_21"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The mesenchymal layer of primitive bladder (mpbl) (syn: primitive bladder mesenchyme) (TS:19-TS:21) is the mesenchyme surrounding the urothelium of primitive bladder. At TS:19-TS:20, expresses Ptch1 and Gli1. From TS:21, contains smooth muscle cells. The mesenchyme of primitive bladder (and later the bladder) is radially patterned due to differentiation of mesenchymal cells into smooth muscle cells. The layers are defined by their location, differing gene expression profiles and proliferation rates.  From TS:20-TS:21 it is divided into inner mesenchyme of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21) and outer mesenchyme of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>primitive bladder mesenchyme</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:30876</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>mesenchymal layer of primitive bladder</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30876"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The mesenchymal layer of primitive bladder (mpbl) (syn: primitive bladder mesenchyme) (TS:19-TS:21) is the mesenchyme surrounding the urothelium of primitive bladder. At TS:19-TS:20, expresses Ptch1 and Gli1. From TS:21, contains smooth muscle cells. The mesenchyme of primitive bladder (and later the bladder) is radially patterned due to differentiation of mesenchymal cells into smooth muscle cells. The layers are defined by their location, differing gene expression profiles and proliferation rates.  From TS:20-TS:21 it is divided into inner mesenchyme of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21) and outer mesenchyme of primitive bladder (TS:20-TS:21).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30879 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30879">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_17379"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_19"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_20"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The caudal urogenital sinus (CUGS) (syn: primitive pelvic urethra) (TS:19-TS:20) is the posterior/caudal part of the urogenital sinus, including the urogenital sinus ridge, where the common nephric ducts/nephric ducts join the urogenital sinus. Comprised of the urogenital sinus ridge, rest of caudal urogenital sinus epithelium and surrounded by the caudal urogenital sinus mesenchyme. Becomes the pelvic urethra at TS:21, which together with the primitive bladder makes up the urogenital sinus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:30879</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>caudal urogenital sinus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30879"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The caudal urogenital sinus (CUGS) (syn: primitive pelvic urethra) (TS:19-TS:20) is the posterior/caudal part of the urogenital sinus, including the urogenital sinus ridge, where the common nephric ducts/nephric ducts join the urogenital sinus. Comprised of the urogenital sinus ridge, rest of caudal urogenital sinus epithelium and surrounded by the caudal urogenital sinus mesenchyme. Becomes the pelvic urethra at TS:21, which together with the primitive bladder makes up the urogenital sinus.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


