    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31505 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31505">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_35965"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30467"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_24"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The proximal urethral meatus of male (prox ur me) (syn: proximal urethral opening of male, urethral duct of male) (TS:21-TS:24) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of male phallic urethra. In males, the proximal urethral meatus of male, is only present up to TS:24. In males from TS:25, the penile urethra has completely canalised and opens at the urethral meatus of penile urethra (syn: urethral opening of male) and the proximal urethral meatus has closed.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>proximal urethral opening of male</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>urethral duct of male</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:31505</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>proximal urethral meatus of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The proximal urethral meatus of male (prox ur me) (syn: proximal urethral opening of male, urethral duct of male) (TS:21-TS:24) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of male phallic urethra. In males, the proximal urethral meatus of male, is only present up to TS:24. In males from TS:25, the penile urethra has completely canalised and opens at the urethral meatus of penile urethra (syn: urethral opening of male) and the proximal urethral meatus has closed.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


