    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31530 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31530">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_35964"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30470"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urethral tube epithelium of female (syn: proximal urethral epithelium of female) is the open, proximal part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female that has canalised into a tube. This structure is distinct from the urethral plate epithelium: when the urethral plate epithelium opens, forming a lumen, it is referred to as the urethral tube epithelium. During development, the tube progresses distally as canalisation progresses distally. First seen at TS:21 in the proximal genital tubercle of female.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>proximal urethral epithelium of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:31530</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urethral tube epithelium of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31530"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urethral tube epithelium of female (syn: proximal urethral epithelium of female) is the open, proximal part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female that has canalised into a tube. This structure is distinct from the urethral plate epithelium: when the urethral plate epithelium opens, forming a lumen, it is referred to as the urethral tube epithelium. During development, the tube progresses distally as canalisation progresses distally. First seen at TS:21 in the proximal genital tubercle of female.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31531 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31531">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_35965"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30470"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_24"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The proximal urethral meatus of female (prox ur me) (syn: proximal urethral opening of female, urethral duct of female) (TS:21-TS:24) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of female phallic urethra (TS:21 to TS:24).  In females, it becomes the proximal urethral meatus of clitoral urethra, part of the epithelium of clitoral urethra from TS:25 to TS:28, and is present to P7. By P8, the proximal urethral meatus is closed in females and the urethra opens at the urethral meatus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>proximal urethral opening of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>urethral duct of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:31531</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>proximal urethral meatus of female</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_31531"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The proximal urethral meatus of female (prox ur me) (syn: proximal urethral opening of female, urethral duct of female) (TS:21-TS:24) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of female phallic urethra (TS:21 to TS:24).  In females, it becomes the proximal urethral meatus of clitoral urethra, part of the epithelium of clitoral urethra from TS:25 to TS:28, and is present to P7. By P8, the proximal urethral meatus is closed in females and the urethra opens at the urethral meatus.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


