                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_28"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The submucosa of ventral pelvic urethra of male (TS:25-TS:28) is the mesenchymal layer located below the muscularis mucosa of pelvic urethra, between the muscularis mucosa and muscle layer of pelvic urethra, comprised of mesenchymal/fibroblastic cells. Marked by Foxf1a mRNA at E17. Can be distinguished from the lamina propria of pelvic urethra as it does not express Snai1 mRNA at E17.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:32298</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>submucosa of ventral pelvic urethra of male</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
