        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urethral gland of penile urethra (TS:27-TS:28). Numerous epithelial urethral glands develop from the epithelium of the urethra. Develop from male urethral gland bud (TS:24-26) and become male urethral gland (TS:27-TS:28) which is subdivided into urethral gland of male pelvic urethra (part of the pelvic urethra) and urethral gland of penile urethra (part of the penile urethra).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:36424</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urethral gland of penile urethra</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36424"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urethral gland of penile urethra (TS:27-TS:28). Numerous epithelial urethral glands develop from the epithelium of the urethra. Develop from male urethral gland bud (TS:24-26) and become male urethral gland (TS:27-TS:28) which is subdivided into urethral gland of male pelvic urethra (part of the pelvic urethra) and urethral gland of penile urethra (part of the penile urethra).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36425 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36425">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_18995"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_24"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_26"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The male urethral gland bud (ugbud) (TS:24-TS:26). Numerous epithelial urethral glands bud from the epithelium of the pelvic urethra. Part of the urethra of male and pelvic urethra of male. Subdivided into anterior and posterior male urethral gland bud (in the male only). In males, anterior male urethral gland buds are also a part of ventral epithelial bud of male, because at early stages, they cannot be distinguished from ventral prostate buds. These two gland types both express the early prostate marker, Nkx3-1.  Edar and Wnt10b mRNA staining intensity can be used to separate prostatic gland buds (High Edar and Wnt10b mRNA expression) from urethral gland buds (Low to not detectable Edar and Wnt10b mRNA) in male mice during development. At TS:27, develop into urethral gland of male pelvic urethra.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:36425</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>male urethral gland bud</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36425"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The male urethral gland bud (ugbud) (TS:24-TS:26). Numerous epithelial urethral glands bud from the epithelium of the pelvic urethra. Part of the urethra of male and pelvic urethra of male. Subdivided into anterior and posterior male urethral gland bud (in the male only). In males, anterior male urethral gland buds are also a part of ventral epithelial bud of male, because at early stages, they cannot be distinguished from ventral prostate buds. These two gland types both express the early prostate marker, Nkx3-1.  Edar and Wnt10b mRNA staining intensity can be used to separate prostatic gland buds (High Edar and Wnt10b mRNA expression) from urethral gland buds (Low to not detectable Edar and Wnt10b mRNA) in male mice during development. At TS:27, develop into urethral gland of male pelvic urethra.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


