    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36451 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36451">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30930"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_25"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002493"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_25"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urethral tube epithelium of clitoral urethra (syn: proximal urethral epithelium of female) (TS:25-25) is the open, proximal part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female that has canalised into a tube. This structure is distinct from the urethral plate epithelium: when the urethral plate epithelium opens, forming a lumen, it is referred to as the urethral tube epithelium. During development, the tube progresses distally as canalisation progresses distally.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>proximal urethral epithelium of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:36451</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urethral tube epithelium of clitoral urethra</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36451"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urethral tube epithelium of clitoral urethra (syn: proximal urethral epithelium of female) (TS:25-25) is the open, proximal part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female that has canalised into a tube. This structure is distinct from the urethral plate epithelium: when the urethral plate epithelium opens, forming a lumen, it is referred to as the urethral tube epithelium. During development, the tube progresses distally as canalisation progresses distally.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36452 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36452">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_37977"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30930"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The proximal urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: proximal urethral opening of female) (TS:25-TS:28) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of clitoral urethra.  Develops from the proximal urethral meatus of female (TS:21-TS:24, part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female).  In females, the proximal urethral meatus remains open to TS:27 (closed by TS:28, p8) and the urethra opens at the urethral meatus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>proximal urethral opening of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:36452</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>proximal urethral meatus of clitoral urethra</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36452"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The proximal urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: proximal urethral opening of female) (TS:25-TS:28) is the proximal opening in the epithelium of clitoral urethra.  Develops from the proximal urethral meatus of female (TS:21-TS:24, part of the epithelium of phallic urethra of female).  In females, the proximal urethral meatus remains open to TS:27 (closed by TS:28, p8) and the urethra opens at the urethral meatus.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36453 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36453">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_37977"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_30930"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002489"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TS_27"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: urethral opening of clitoral urethra, distal urethral opening of female) (TS:27-TS:28) is the opening of the clitoral urethra, located within the clitoris. The clitoral urethra is open proximally at the proximal urethral meatus (present to P7) (syn: proximal urethral opening of female or urethral duct) located at the base of the clitoris. The proximal urethral meatus closes after birth (closed by P8). In adults and from birth, the urethra of female is open externally at the urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: distal urethral opening of female) which is anatomically located within the clitoris. (This is different to humans, where the urethral opening is located between the clitoris and vagina).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>anatomical_structure</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>distal urethral opening of female</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>urethral opening of clitoral urethra</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>EMAPA:36453</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>urethral meatus of clitoral urethra</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/EMAPA_36453"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: urethral opening of clitoral urethra, distal urethral opening of female) (TS:27-TS:28) is the opening of the clitoral urethra, located within the clitoris. The clitoral urethra is open proximally at the proximal urethral meatus (present to P7) (syn: proximal urethral opening of female or urethral duct) located at the base of the clitoris. The proximal urethral meatus closes after birth (closed by P8). In adults and from birth, the urethra of female is open externally at the urethral meatus of clitoral urethra (syn: distal urethral opening of female) which is anatomically located within the clitoris. (This is different to humans, where the urethral opening is located between the clitoris and vagina).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25968320</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


